但你知道的，早期的斯皮尔伯格电影里，那些房子都很有生活气息。

705
00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:02.840
And if it's not lived in, I can't buy into it.
如果感觉没人住过，我就无法代入。

706
00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:03.880
Yeah.
对。

707
00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:05.180
If it doesn't feel real.
如果没有真实感的话。

708
00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:10.240
You know, sometimes you watch a sitcom or, and everything's so clean.
你知道，有时你看情景喜剧或者别的，一切都太干净了。

709
00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:10.880
Squeaky.
一尘不染。

710
00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:13.460
And you can tell it's on a stage.
一眼就能看出是在摄影棚里拍的。

711
00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.280
And I don't like it.
我可不喜欢这样。

712
00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:18.780
You know, I like it when it's like lived in, is what I'm saying.
你知道的，我就喜欢那种有生活气息的，我的意思是这样。

713
00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:23.020
The production designer on Nimrods, Adam Reamer, was a genius.
《笨蛋爱找茬》的制作设计亚当·雷默是个天才。

714
00:22:23.720 --> 00:22:24.160
Yes.
没错。

715
00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.360
Like the home, the garage, all the sets.
比如家里、车库，所有的布景。

716
00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:29.600
I've never seen you in a role like this before.
我从没见过你演过这样的角色。

717
00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:31.080
As a mom.
扮演一位母亲。

718
00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:31.840
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

719
00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:33.440
Oh, well, you know.
哦，好吧，你知道的。

720
00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:34.780
Well, you were a mom on Split Yourself.
不过，你在《分裂自我》里演过妈妈。

721
00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:36.120
I split them together.
我把它们拼到一块儿了。

722
00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:37.260
Except for that.
除了那部之外。

723
00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:38.400
Except for that sitcom.
除了那部情景喜剧。

724
00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:40.580
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

725
00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:41.740
We're on a sitcom together.
我们一起演过情景喜剧。

726
00:22:41.820 --> 00:22:41.980
Yeah.
对。

727
00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:44.100
But to your point, it's a different kind of role.
但正如你所说，这是个不同类型的角色。

728
00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:47.260
And I mean, I could get personal.
我是说，我可以谈点私事。

729
00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:48.840
Oh, my God.
天哪。

730
00:22:48.940 --> 00:22:49.480
Get personal.
谈点私事吧。

731
00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:50.220
Should I?
我要说吗？

732
00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:50.780
Yes.
说吧。

733
00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:55.500
So, I shot this movie two weeks after I had my port removed.
我是在摘除输液港两周后拍这部电影的。

734
00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:57.880
After having gone through all my cancer treatment.
在经历了我所有的癌症治疗之后。

735
00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:00.040
I had my last infusion.
我做了最后一次输液。

736
00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:06.260
And I'd been kind of like living in my house for like a year.
我差不多在家里闷头呆了一年左右。

737
00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:06.960
You know?
你知道吗？

738
00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:09.860
Because I was a little bit on my own personal lockdown.
因为我有点像是在经历个人的居家隔离。

739
00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:12.120
Where my life was just about the treatments.
当时我的生活全都是围绕着治疗转。

740
00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:17.840
And I had my last immunotherapy infusion early in 2025.
我在2025年年初做了最后一次免疫治疗输液。

741
00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:20.560
And then I got my port removed.
然后我拆了输液港。

742
00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:23.160
And two weeks later, I was on set shooting this movie.
两周后，我就在片场拍这部电影了。

743
00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:29.320
And from that experience, I had a kind of heaviness in me.
从那次经历中，我心里有一种沉重感。

744
00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.180
Because a lot had happened to me in that year.
因为那一年我经历了太多事。

745
00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:33.540
I had a literal heaviness.
我是说字面意义上的沉重感。

746
00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:35.600
I gained 15 pounds during chemo.
化疗期间我胖了15磅。

747
00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:37.280
And during all my treatment.
还有在整个治疗期间。

748
00:23:37.820 --> 00:23:40.360
And my hair had just started to grow back.
我的头发才刚开始长出来。

749
00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:42.240
Like, I had just enough for this movie.
差不多刚好够拍这部电影。

750
00:23:42.380 --> 00:23:43.260
That's my real hair.
那可是我的真发。

751
00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:44.440
People have asked if it was a wig.
人们曾问过这是不是假发。

752
00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:45.940
But I had just enough hair.
但我刚刚好有那么多头发。

753
00:23:46.060 --> 00:23:47.280
They kind of like brushed it forward.
他们差不多是把它往前梳了梳。

754
00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:48.060
They were brilliant.
他们太棒了。

755
00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:53.500
And it was such a gift to me to take that and put it into this part.
对我来说，能把这些经历融入这个角色，真是一份厚礼。

756
00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.620
This part of this mom who also has a real heaviness to her.
一个同样有着沉重负担的母亲的角色。

757
00:23:57.760 --> 00:23:58.420
She's a widow.
她是个寡妇。

758
00:23:58.740 --> 00:24:01.800
She's raising two teen boys on her own.
她独自抚养两个十几岁的男孩。

759
00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:04.480
And she's a little bit at the end of her rope.
她有点走投无路了。

760
00:24:04.620 --> 00:24:06.800
But trying to be kind of optimistic at the same time.
但同时又努力保持乐观。

761
00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.060
I mean, I love this woman.
我是说，我很爱这个女人。

762
00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:12.540
And I don't think this is a part that I would have been offered or asked to play
而且我觉得，如果不是因为我经历过那些风雨，

763
00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:15.180
had I not gone through everything I went through.
这个角色是绝不会有人找我或让我来演的。

764
00:24:15.340 --> 00:24:16.600
Because I didn't have it in me.
因为我当时没有这种能力。

765
00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:17.800
I didn't have it in my body.
我的身体里没有这种体验。

766
00:24:17.980 --> 00:24:19.440
I didn't have it in my toolkit.
我的百宝箱里没有这个工具。

767
00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:20.640
Like, I just didn't have it.
就是说，我真的没有。

768
00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:24.300
And so, for me, this movie is really, really special.
所以对我和这部电影来说，这真的、真的很特别。

769
00:24:24.460 --> 00:24:29.540
Because I got to take something hard that happened to me.
因为我把我身上发生过的艰难遭遇，

770
00:24:29.680 --> 00:24:31.400
And I got to put it into art.
转化为了艺术。

771
00:24:31.640 --> 00:24:34.280
Which is kind of just the best thing ever.
这可以说是最棒的事情了。

772
00:24:34.500 --> 00:24:35.920
And it was really healing for me.
这对我也真的起到了疗愈作用。

773
00:24:36.400 --> 00:24:38.100
So, thank you for saying that.
所以，谢谢你这么说。

774
00:24:38.280 --> 00:24:39.180
It really means a lot.
这对我意义重大。

775
00:24:40.060 --> 00:24:41.400
I just, I'm sorry.
我只是，我很抱歉。

776
00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:42.220
Aw.
噢。

777
00:24:42.740 --> 00:24:44.140
I remember you telling me.
我记得你跟我说过。

778
00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:45.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

779
00:24:45.060 --> 00:24:45.540
On set.
在片场。

780
00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:46.560
It was devastating.
那太令人痛心了。

781
00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:47.460
Yeah.
是啊。

782
00:24:47.460 --> 00:24:48.100
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

783
00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:48.880
Yeah.
对。

784
00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:50.240
Yeah, I'm so sorry.
是啊，我真的很遗憾。

785
00:24:50.640 --> 00:24:51.300
But you're...
但你……

786
00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:52.620
I'm in full remission.
我已经完全康复了。

787
00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:53.040
Yes.
是的。

788
00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:53.460
Yeah.
对。

789
00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:55.380
And now it's like, it's good.
现在感觉就像是，一切都好。

790
00:24:55.880 --> 00:24:58.420
God, it's weird to say it was a good thing that happened to me.
天哪，说发生在我身上的事是一件好事，感觉有点怪。

791
00:24:58.480 --> 00:25:01.540
But it was definitely one of those moments in life.
但这绝对是生命中那几个关键时刻之一。

792
00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.420
It was a before and after.
这是一个分水岭。

793
00:25:03.760 --> 00:25:04.400
You know?
你知道吗？

794
00:25:04.580 --> 00:25:06.040
There's like, there was my life before.
就像是，曾有过我以前的生活。

795
00:25:06.200 --> 00:25:07.920
And now there's my life after.
而现在有了我以后的生活。

796
00:25:08.780 --> 00:25:12.140
And my life after, it's been transformative.
而我以后的生活，经历了脱胎换骨的改变。

797
00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:14.140
I can't.
我快说不下去了。

798
00:25:14.240 --> 00:25:14.460
Yeah.
是啊。

799
00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:19.700
But I mean, I feel like you must have had before and after with getting sober.
不过我是说，我觉得你戒酒的经历也一定是个分水岭。

800
00:25:19.880 --> 00:25:20.060
Yeah.
对。

801
00:25:20.060 --> 00:25:20.600
Right?
对吧？

802
00:25:20.860 --> 00:25:21.020
Yeah.
是啊。

803
00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:22.400
I mean, that's a very before or after.
我是说，这分明就是个“前后对比”嘛。

804
00:25:22.420 --> 00:25:22.960
I think it's different though.
不过我觉得还是不太一样。

805
00:25:24.440 --> 00:25:27.880
I don't think I was as scared as you might have been.
我觉得我当时可能没你那么害怕。

806
00:25:28.040 --> 00:25:31.240
You know, I always thought, you know, I can always get sober or whatever.
你知道的，我总是觉得，你知道，我随时都能戒酒什么的。

807
00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:33.440
I mean, that's all I needed to do is to get sober.
我是说，我当时只需要把酒戒了就行。

808
00:25:33.620 --> 00:25:33.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

809
00:25:33.880 --> 00:25:34.140
Right?
对吧？

810
00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:37.560
But you have no control over what you had, you know?
但你完全无法控制你所得的病，你知道吗？

811
00:25:37.760 --> 00:25:39.920
So, it must be just terrifying.
所以，那一定非常可怕。

812
00:25:40.540 --> 00:25:40.700
Yeah.
是啊。

813
00:25:41.120 --> 00:25:45.660
You know, truly, it's really hard to watch someone you love go through something and you
你知道，真的，看着你爱的人经历磨难，而你却

814
00:25:45.660 --> 00:25:46.500
don't know how to help them.
不知道该怎么帮他们，这种感觉真的很艰难。

815
00:25:46.600 --> 00:25:46.800
Yeah.
是啊。

816
00:25:47.380 --> 00:25:52.880
And so, and anything you do to try to help doesn't feel like enough, you know?
所以，你无论做什么去帮忙都觉得还远远不够，你知道吗？

817
00:25:53.060 --> 00:25:55.360
And so, you just try to show up, you know?
所以，你只能尽量陪伴在身边，你知道吗？

818
00:25:55.560 --> 00:25:55.860
Yeah.
是啊。

819
00:25:55.860 --> 00:26:01.540
And so, even as you were saying all that, it was so great to watch this movie and have seen
所以，即使在你刚才说那些话的时候，看这部电影，看到你挺过来并走出了阴霾、还能继续创作，这种感觉真的很棒。

820
00:26:01.540 --> 00:26:04.240
you through that and on the other side and getting to create.
而且我很喜欢这个角色，也很喜欢李拍的这部电影。

821
00:26:04.460 --> 00:26:07.980
And I love the character and I love the movie that Lee made.
真的非常棒。

822
00:26:08.120 --> 00:26:08.660
It's really great.
是啊。

823
00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:08.920
Yeah.
我很期待大家看到它。

824
00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:10.200
I'm excited for people to see it.
真的吗？

825
00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:14.980
Well, lady, you took me to get my port removed because Lee had started shooting the movie.
话说回来，当时李开始拍电影了，你陪我去拆了化疗港。

826
00:26:15.320 --> 00:26:15.520
Yeah.
是啊。

827
00:26:15.520 --> 00:26:19.440
It was a weird thing for us too because he'd been with me the whole journey and now his
对我们来说这也是一件挺奇妙的事，因为他一路都陪着我，结果在

828
00:26:19.440 --> 00:26:24.240
movie gets greenlit in like the last two months of my treatment and he had to be away.
我治疗的最后两个月左右，他的电影获准立项了，他不得不离开。

829
00:26:24.740 --> 00:26:28.500
And so, Angela took me to get my port removed.
所以，安吉拉陪我去拆了化疗港。

830
00:26:28.700 --> 00:26:28.920
Yeah.
是啊。

831
00:26:29.240 --> 00:26:29.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

832
00:26:29.660 --> 00:26:32.480
Which was amazing because she's the best BFF ever.
这太棒了，因为她是有史以来最好的闺蜜。

833
00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:32.980
Yeah.
是啊。

834
00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:33.560
We're family.
我们是一家人。

835
00:26:33.860 --> 00:26:33.960
Yeah.
是啊。

836
00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:34.300
Yeah.
是啊。

837
00:26:34.460 --> 00:26:34.980
That's amazing.
太棒了。

838
00:26:35.180 --> 00:26:36.220
So, you take care of each other.
所以你们会互相照顾。

839
00:26:36.260 --> 00:26:38.100
I don't think I have anyone like that in my life.
我觉得我生命中没有这样的人。

840
00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:38.940
Maybe I'm a girlfriend.
也许我算个女朋友吧。

841
00:26:40.360 --> 00:26:41.540
Sure, your girlfriend.
当然，你的女朋友。

842
00:26:42.340 --> 00:26:42.700
Yeah.
是啊。

843
00:26:42.880 --> 00:26:44.380
Maybe I'm a girlfriend.
也许我算个女朋友吧。

844
00:26:44.580 --> 00:26:45.100
Your girlfriend.
你的女朋友。

845
00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:46.920
She would take you to LAX, right?
她会送你去洛杉矶国际机场，对吧？

846
00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:49.800
I don't think so, but I think that she would for port.
我觉得不会，但我猜她会为了化疗港送我。

847
00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:50.140
I don't know.
我不知道。

848
00:26:50.280 --> 00:26:50.440
Yeah.
是啊。

849
00:26:50.620 --> 00:26:50.780
Yeah.
是啊。

850
00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:52.040
But Santino, I don't know.
不过桑蒂诺，我可说不准。

851
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:54.180
Andrew Santino, I don't know.
安德鲁·桑蒂诺，我不知道。

852
00:26:54.600 --> 00:26:56.960
I'm not sure Lee would drive me to LAX.
我不确定李会不会开车送我去洛杉矶国际机场。

853
00:26:58.320 --> 00:27:03.180
He'll see me through cancer treatment and I'm not sure he's dropping me at LAX or picking
他陪我度过了癌症治疗期，但我不敢确定他是否会送我去洛杉矶国际机场或是接

854
00:27:03.180 --> 00:27:03.640
me up.
我回来。

855
00:27:03.820 --> 00:27:06.880
For people listening, LAX is the worst airport to try to drive.
对于听众朋友们，洛杉矶国际机场是开车最难的机场。

856
00:27:06.880 --> 00:27:07.200
It's the worSt.
简直糟透了。

857
00:27:07.360 --> 00:27:08.020
Burbank, yes.
伯班克机场，可以。

858
00:27:08.340 --> 00:27:08.740
Burbank?
伯班克吗？

859
00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:09.640
Yes, for sure.
对，肯定的。

860
00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:10.360
Oh, he's taking me to Burbank.
噢，他会带我去伯班克。

861
00:27:10.360 --> 00:27:11.080
Burbank is fine.
伯班克挺好的。

862
00:27:11.220 --> 00:27:11.720
All the time.
经常去。

863
00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.660
I would take you to the Long Beach airport.
我会带你去长滩机场。

864
00:27:13.880 --> 00:27:14.340
I would do that.
我愿意这么做。

865
00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:15.280
Yes, yes, yes.
对，对，对。

866
00:27:15.460 --> 00:27:16.700
But LAX, man.
但洛杉矶国际机场嘛。

867
00:27:17.040 --> 00:27:18.280
Wait, back to Nimrods.
等等，回到《呆头鹅》这部电影。

868
00:27:18.360 --> 00:27:18.920
Yes, of course.
对，当然。

869
00:27:24.240 --> 00:27:24.900
We're offered this part.
我们得到了这个角色。

870
00:27:25.020 --> 00:27:25.900
And I said, yes, immediately.
我立刻就答应了。

871
00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:27.360
There you go.
就是这样。

872
00:27:27.520 --> 00:27:32.020
Because I knew Billy from a long time ago during my mad TV days.
因为我很久以前在《疯狂电视》的时候就认识比利了。

873
00:27:32.340 --> 00:27:35.560
Billy Joe Armstrong from Green Day, producer of this movie.
来自绿日乐队的比利·乔·阿姆斯壮，这部电影的制片人。

874
00:27:35.860 --> 00:27:36.080
Yeah.
对。

875
00:27:36.200 --> 00:27:37.740
And I used to hang out with him.
我以前经常跟他一起玩。

876
00:27:37.820 --> 00:27:39.040
I run into him, hang out with him.
我会偶遇他，跟他一起玩。

877
00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:41.020
Back then, LA was different.
那时候，洛杉矶可不一样。

878
00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:44.440
Like, I remember going to Baja Fresh and then running into the Strokes.
比如，我记得我去过巴哈新鲜墨西哥餐厅，然后遇到了击打乐队。

879
00:27:44.740 --> 00:27:45.180
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

880
00:27:45.220 --> 00:27:46.480
You just run into people.
你随时都会偶遇各种人。

881
00:27:46.580 --> 00:27:47.140
That's so cool.
那太酷了。

882
00:27:47.140 --> 00:27:49.040
What was your first neighborhood in LA?
你在洛杉矶住的第一个社区是哪里？

883
00:27:49.380 --> 00:27:54.620
It was North Hollywood, then Silver Lake, then West Hollywood, then Hollywood, and now
是北好莱坞，然后是银湖，然后是西好莱坞，然后是好莱坞，现在是

884
00:27:54.620 --> 00:27:55.180
Studio City.
工作室城。

885
00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:55.680
Yeah.
对。

886
00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:56.820
So I've been around.
所以我到处都住过。

887
00:27:57.100 --> 00:27:58.220
Where were you in West Hollywood?
你以前在西好莱坞哪里？

888
00:27:58.500 --> 00:28:00.440
I lived above the comedy store.
我住在喜剧商店上面。

889
00:28:00.740 --> 00:28:01.400
Polly owned it.
波莉是房东。

890
00:28:01.560 --> 00:28:02.160
Are you serious?
真的吗？

891
00:28:02.300 --> 00:28:02.640
Oh, yeah.
噢，是的。

892
00:28:03.020 --> 00:28:03.920
What was that like?
那是种什么体验？

893
00:28:03.920 --> 00:28:04.420
It was terrible.
太糟糕了。

894
00:28:04.540 --> 00:28:05.180
I mean, I-
我的意思是，我——

895
00:28:05.180 --> 00:28:06.100
It was a human nightmare.
简直是一场人间噩梦。

896
00:28:06.460 --> 00:28:08.040
That seems really difficult.
听起来真的很不容易。

897
00:28:08.300 --> 00:28:08.940
I would come home.
我回到家。

898
00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:10.020
He'd be on my bed sleeping.
他竟然躺在我的床上睡觉。

899
00:28:10.360 --> 00:28:11.400
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

900
00:28:11.540 --> 00:28:12.060
Polly, sure.
波莉，没错。

901
00:28:12.460 --> 00:28:12.660
Yeah.
对啊。

902
00:28:12.940 --> 00:28:14.740
Dude, I am the house, brah.
老兄，我就是这房子的老大，兄弟。

903
00:28:15.340 --> 00:28:15.640
Right?
对吧？

904
00:28:15.640 --> 00:28:17.440
I can sleep wherever I want to sleep.
我想在哪睡就在哪睡。

905
00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:19.500
I go, I pay rent!
我去，我交房租的！

906
00:28:20.900 --> 00:28:21.300
Dude?
老兄？

907
00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:22.940
Yeah, I pay rent.
对，我交房租。

908
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:28.160
But anyway, so I moved out of there because the house is falling off a cliff, they said.
不过总之，我从那搬出来了，因为他们说那房子快掉下悬崖了。

909
00:28:28.720 --> 00:28:29.680
The comedy store?
喜剧商店？

910
00:28:29.780 --> 00:28:29.960
The house?
那栋房子？

911
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.260
No, no.
不，不。

912
00:28:30.340 --> 00:28:34.920
So the house above the comedy store, the inspector came in and goes, you could die in here.
喜剧商店上面的那栋房子，检查员来检查后说，你们在这可能会送命。

913
00:28:35.760 --> 00:28:38.840
And then I remember a bunch of comics were like, just buy a house.
然后我记得一帮喜剧演员就说，买套房子呗。

914
00:28:38.840 --> 00:28:39.780
You can buy a house.
你可以买套房子的。

915
00:28:39.860 --> 00:28:40.960
So I bought my first house.
所以我买了我的第一套房子。

916
00:28:41.300 --> 00:28:41.700
Nice.
不错。

917
00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:42.520
After that, yeah.
在那之后，对。

918
00:28:43.100 --> 00:28:45.480
Which is freeing in many ways.
在很多方面这都让人感到解脱。

919
00:28:45.640 --> 00:28:46.540
It feels grown up.
感觉像是成年了。

920
00:28:46.820 --> 00:28:46.960
Yeah.
对。

921
00:28:47.200 --> 00:28:48.560
And back then, you could afford it.
而且那时候，你还买得起。

922
00:28:48.640 --> 00:28:49.200
Now you can't.
现在可买不起了。

923
00:28:49.440 --> 00:28:50.100
No, now it's crazy.
对，现在太离谱了。

924
00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:50.740
Yeah, now you can't.
是啊，现在根本买不起。

925
00:28:50.740 --> 00:28:51.680
But yeah, now it's crazy.
不过对，现在太疯狂了。

926
00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:52.180
Okay, wait.
好吧，等等。

927
00:28:52.260 --> 00:28:53.220
There's one thing I have to tell you.
我有一件事必须告诉你。

928
00:28:53.380 --> 00:28:55.480
I really want to come see your-
我真的很想去看你的……

929
00:28:55.480 --> 00:28:55.640
No.
不。

930
00:28:55.920 --> 00:28:56.480
Stage show.
舞台表演。

931
00:28:56.740 --> 00:28:57.020
No.
不。

932
00:28:57.160 --> 00:28:57.440
And then-
然后——

933
00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.320
What do you mean stage show?
你什么意思，舞台表演？

934
00:28:58.420 --> 00:28:58.860
Stand up?
单口喜剧？

935
00:28:58.980 --> 00:28:59.260
Yes.
对。

936
00:28:59.620 --> 00:28:59.980
Dude.
老兄。

937
00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:01.400
Yeah, it's just stand up.
对，就是单口喜剧。

938
00:29:01.740 --> 00:29:01.900
No.
不。

939
00:29:01.900 --> 00:29:04.020
I have a special coming out on Hulu in November.
我有一个专场要在十一月份登录Hulu。

940
00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:04.420
Okay.
好吧。

941
00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:06.040
It's my first hour special.
这是我的第一个一小时专场。

942
00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:06.620
I know.
我知道。

943
00:29:06.780 --> 00:29:07.960
It's your first hour special.
这是你的第一个一小时专场。

944
00:29:08.220 --> 00:29:08.580
That's amazing.
太棒了。

945
00:29:08.640 --> 00:29:09.260
For what company?
在哪家公司？

946
00:29:09.500 --> 00:29:09.840
Hulu.
Hulu。

947
00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:10.620
Okay, good.
行，很好。

948
00:29:10.660 --> 00:29:11.420
I was listening.
我有在听。

949
00:29:11.420 --> 00:29:11.720
Okay.
好吧。

950
00:29:11.980 --> 00:29:13.800
But my sons love you.
不过我的儿子们都很喜欢你。

951
00:29:13.860 --> 00:29:16.940
And they were so tickled that I was meeting you today.
而且他们听说我今天要见你，高兴得不得了。

952
00:29:17.040 --> 00:29:19.100
They just can't believe that you're in the podcaSt.
他们简直不敢相信你要上播客。

953
00:29:19.100 --> 00:29:19.520
Were they?
是吗？

954
00:29:19.580 --> 00:29:20.040
Are they here?
他们来了吗？

955
00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.320
No, they're at home.
没有，他们在家里。

956
00:29:21.480 --> 00:29:21.700
Okay.
好吧。

957
00:29:21.980 --> 00:29:23.320
But my nephew-
不过我的侄子——

958
00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:23.780
You're a big deal.
你现在可是个大人物了。

959
00:29:23.980 --> 00:29:26.060
You met my nephew on the set of Nimrod.
你在《捣蛋鬼》的片场见过我侄子。

960
00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:26.460
Yes.
是的。

961
00:29:26.620 --> 00:29:29.640
He flew out because he wanted to see a couple days of filming.
他特意飞过来，想看几天拍摄。

962
00:29:29.840 --> 00:29:30.740
It's because of you.
这都是因为你。

963
00:29:31.280 --> 00:29:32.140
Was I nice to him?
我对她好吗？

964
00:29:32.320 --> 00:29:32.840
Yes, very.
对，非常好。

965
00:29:33.080 --> 00:29:34.220
Because I'm a nice person.
因为我是个好人。

966
00:29:34.220 --> 00:29:35.340
Yes, you are.
对，你是的。

967
00:29:35.580 --> 00:29:35.740
Exactly.
没错。

968
00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:38.000
He was so excited to meet you, and that was so nice of you.
他能见到你特别兴奋，你人真的太好了。

969
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:38.620
Stage show?
舞台剧？

970
00:29:39.140 --> 00:29:41.720
I sometimes get phrases wrong, just a little bit.
我有时会把一些词语弄错，就一点点。

971
00:29:41.800 --> 00:29:42.740
I want to brag on you.
我想夸夸你。

972
00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:44.280
I want to talk about what a nice person you are.
我想说说你是个多好的人。

973
00:29:44.760 --> 00:29:46.600
I hope this won't be embarrassing to you.
希望这不会让你觉得尴尬。

974
00:29:46.720 --> 00:29:47.700
I don't think it would be.
我觉得不会。

975
00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:51.780
Okay, so there's a young guy in this movie, Ryan FauSt.
好，这部电影里有个年轻小伙子，瑞安·福斯特。

976
00:29:52.140 --> 00:29:52.640
Love him.
我可太喜欢他了。

977
00:29:52.760 --> 00:29:55.820
He plays the drummer in the young punk band.
他在那支年轻朋克乐队里演鼓手。

978
00:29:55.980 --> 00:29:56.580
Yeah, I understand.
对，我明白。

979
00:29:56.800 --> 00:29:57.380
He's so great.
他太棒了。

980
00:29:57.560 --> 00:29:58.920
I'm letting other people know.
我正跟别人说呢。

981
00:29:59.020 --> 00:29:59.400
Uh-oh.
呃哦。

982
00:29:59.800 --> 00:30:02.120
This guy, first of all, he's just so good in the movie.
这家伙，首先，他在电影里表现得太棒了。

983
00:30:02.180 --> 00:30:02.920
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

984
00:30:02.920 --> 00:30:04.260
He's so good in the movie.
他在电影里演得太好了。

985
00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:05.160
So good in the movie.
在电影里演得太好了。

986
00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:05.500
He's so good.
他太棒了。

987
00:30:05.880 --> 00:30:10.220
And he had to learn to play the drums because he's really playing.
而且他必须学打鼓，因为他是真在打。

988
00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:12.080
I think they all had to learn, right?
我想他们都得学，对吧？

989
00:30:12.340 --> 00:30:12.700
Yes.
对。

990
00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:15.260
Well, Kyler Kaufman already knew how to play guitar.
嗯，凯勒·考夫曼本来就会弹吉他。

991
00:30:15.460 --> 00:30:19.620
But yes, Mason Tames had to learn to play guitar, and then Ryan had to learn druMs.
不过对，梅森·坦姆斯得学弹吉他，然后瑞安得学打鼓。

992
00:30:19.620 --> 00:30:21.300
And he was really dedicated.
而且他真的很投入。

993
00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:23.360
Yeah, because he's a student of acting.
对，因为他是个表演专业的学生。

994
00:30:23.540 --> 00:30:23.660
Yeah.
对。

995
00:30:23.660 --> 00:30:26.560
He wants to immerse himself into the role and not look fake.
他想让自己完全沉浸在角色中，不想显得假。

996
00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:31.940
And that's what I love about Ryan is that he's brave, and he commits.
这就是我喜欢瑞安的地方，他很勇敢，而且全心投入。

997
00:30:31.980 --> 00:30:33.360
And I know what the compliment is.
我知道这个赞美是什么了。

998
00:30:33.440 --> 00:30:33.800
You do?
你知道？

999
00:30:33.940 --> 00:30:35.140
And I don't think it's a compliment.
而且我觉得这算不上什么赞美。

1000
00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:37.600
And I don't think it's me being a nice guy.
而且我觉得这并不是因为我是个好人。

1001
00:30:38.140 --> 00:30:40.120
It's just that I like bravery.
我只是喜欢勇敢的人。

1002
00:30:40.700 --> 00:30:41.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1003
00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:44.700
And Ryan said to me on set, I want to try stand-up.
瑞安在片场对我说，我想试试单口喜剧。

1004
00:30:44.840 --> 00:30:45.840
Is that what you're getting at?
这就是你想表达的意思吗？

1005
00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:50.100
You said, you write a set, let's set a date, and I'll let you open for me.
你说，你写一段稿子，我们定个日子，我让你给我暖场。

1006
00:30:50.360 --> 00:30:50.660
Yeah.
对。

1007
00:30:51.520 --> 00:30:52.200
That's what I said.
我是这么说的。

1008
00:30:52.420 --> 00:30:52.700
Yeah.
对。

1009
00:30:52.840 --> 00:30:53.000
Yeah.
对。

1010
00:30:53.200 --> 00:30:54.640
I mean, that's f***ing cool.
我的意思是，这真的太酷了。

1011
00:30:54.820 --> 00:30:55.860
And he did it a bunch of times.
而且他演了好多次。

1012
00:30:56.020 --> 00:30:56.460
I know.
我知道。

1013
00:30:56.560 --> 00:30:57.420
Yeah, and he was very good.
对，而且他表现得非常好。

1014
00:30:57.980 --> 00:31:01.720
And that kind of like mentorship, like that is so cool.
这种像导师一样的提携，真的太棒了。

1015
00:31:01.940 --> 00:31:02.780
That is so cool.
真的太棒了。

1016
00:31:02.860 --> 00:31:03.900
Yeah, I've done that a lot.
对，我经常这么做。

1017
00:31:04.080 --> 00:31:08.400
But it's like, I just love people that are brave and that walk through fear.
但我就是喜欢那些勇敢、敢于面对恐惧的人。

1018
00:31:08.500 --> 00:31:11.780
And I'm willing to hold someone's hand to do that.
我愿意为了这个去拉着别人的手。

1019
00:31:11.960 --> 00:31:12.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1020
00:31:12.280 --> 00:31:15.420
You know, but yeah, I'm not one of those guys that are like completely jealous
你知道的，但我也不是那种完全心怀嫉妒的人

1021
00:31:15.420 --> 00:31:17.320
or I want people to make it.
或者我希望别人能成功。

1022
00:31:17.860 --> 00:31:18.680
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

1023
00:31:18.940 --> 00:31:19.280
That's a beautiful thing.
这是一件美好的事。

1024
00:31:19.420 --> 00:31:22.620
Because it's, I mean, you know, in order to achieve success,
因为，我的意思是，你知道的，为了取得成功，

1025
00:31:22.620 --> 00:31:24.840
you have to help people achieve the success, I believe.
我相信你必须帮助别人取得成功。

1026
00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:26.480
And people probably helped you.
而且以前可能也有人帮助过你。

1027
00:31:27.220 --> 00:31:27.640
Yeah.
对。

1028
00:31:27.940 --> 00:31:28.120
Yeah.
对。

1029
00:31:28.280 --> 00:31:28.600
They did.
确实如此。

1030
00:31:28.780 --> 00:31:28.900
Yeah.
对。

1031
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:31.720
I think the Shore family was very vital, you know.
我觉得肖尔家族非常关键，你知道的。

1032
00:31:31.860 --> 00:31:33.820
Polly's mom owned the comedy store.
波利的妈妈开了喜剧商店。

1033
00:31:34.560 --> 00:31:39.280
And she saw me do open mic, and then she saw me open for her son,
她看我做开放麦，然后看我为她儿子暖场，

1034
00:31:39.300 --> 00:31:41.780
and she made me a paid regular, and I moved to L.A.
她让我成了有偿常驻演员，然后我搬到了洛杉矶。

1035
00:31:41.920 --> 00:31:43.080
This is in San Diego.
这是在圣地亚哥。

1036
00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:43.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1037
00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:47.900
And so it really helped, and a lot of comics helped, you know.
所以这真的很有帮助，而且很多喜剧演员也帮了忙，你知道的。

1038
00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:51.520
And Dice Clay helped in a weird way, you know.
迪斯·克莱也以一种奇怪的方式帮了忙，你知道的。

1039
00:31:51.620 --> 00:31:54.480
People really kind of pulled me up on my sleeves.
人们真的是拉了我一把。

1040
00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:55.640
Is that the term, or?
是这个词吗，还是？

1041
00:31:55.780 --> 00:31:56.460
I don't know.
我不知道。

1042
00:31:58.380 --> 00:32:00.140
But people took a chance on you.
但人们给了你机会。

1043
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:00.660
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

1044
00:32:00.800 --> 00:32:00.980
Right?
对吧？

1045
00:32:01.220 --> 00:32:02.420
People helped you, no?
人们帮助了你，不是吗？

1046
00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:02.980
Of course.
当然。

1047
00:32:03.060 --> 00:32:03.620
Yeah, of course.
对，当然。

1048
00:32:03.700 --> 00:32:03.960
Yeah.
对。

1049
00:32:04.020 --> 00:32:04.740
And this is the thing.
事情就是这样。

1050
00:32:04.860 --> 00:32:07.520
Like, this is, I love that about our industry,
比如，这就是，我非常喜欢我们行业这一点，

1051
00:32:07.520 --> 00:32:09.760
when you find those other people who are like that,
当你找到那些和你志同道合的人，

1052
00:32:09.760 --> 00:32:11.920
I believe there's enough room for everyone.
我相信每个人的空间都绰绰有余。

1053
00:32:12.060 --> 00:32:12.280
Yeah.
没错。

1054
00:32:12.480 --> 00:32:14.500
And if you've got a talent, we've got room for you.
只要你有才华，我们这里就有你的容身之所。

1055
00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:15.980
Yes, I do believe that, too.
是的，我也这么认为。

1056
00:32:16.180 --> 00:32:17.740
And it's like, I'll tell you something.
而且就像是，我跟你说个事。

1057
00:32:17.900 --> 00:32:20.360
I was plagued by jealousy early on in my career.
我在职业生涯的早期深受嫉妒的困扰。

1058
00:32:20.580 --> 00:32:20.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1059
00:32:21.560 --> 00:32:25.040
I did have a moment where I was like, what about me?
我确实有过那么一刻，心想：那我呢？

1060
00:32:25.600 --> 00:32:28.260
And then, you know, about a year of that, I was like,
然后呢，你知道的，经历了一年左右的那种状态，我想：

1061
00:32:28.360 --> 00:32:32.600
this is not who I am, and it's painful.
这根本不是真正的我，而且这种感觉太痛苦了。

1062
00:32:33.020 --> 00:32:33.300
Yeah.
是的。

1063
00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:34.060
To live in that.
活在那种情绪里。

1064
00:32:34.220 --> 00:32:34.340
Yeah.
是的。

1065
00:32:34.340 --> 00:32:35.580
You know, I have to admit that, you know.
你知道的，我不得不承认这一点。

1066
00:32:35.580 --> 00:32:37.260
But, yeah, I'm completely different now.
不过，是的，我现在完全不同了。

1067
00:32:38.040 --> 00:32:38.300
Yeah.
是的。

1068
00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:39.420
Abundant universe.
宇宙资源是丰饶的。

1069
00:32:39.520 --> 00:32:40.700
You kind of come to that.
你多少都会领悟到这一点。

1070
00:32:40.840 --> 00:32:42.100
And I think if you get older.
而且我觉得随着年龄的增长。

1071
00:32:42.360 --> 00:32:47.920
I think that to survive in this biz,
我觉得要在这一行生存下来，

1072
00:32:48.980 --> 00:32:50.760
and also, can I just say this, too?
还有，我能顺便说一句吗？

1073
00:32:50.980 --> 00:32:54.760
You're adapting to the transitions of show business.
你正在适应演艺圈的变迁。

1074
00:32:55.240 --> 00:32:58.200
Like, for me, it's like, I saw the writing on the wall a little bit.
比如对我来说，就是，我稍微预感到了未来的趋势。

1075
00:32:58.200 --> 00:32:59.840
I was like, I have to create my own thing.
我当时就想：我必须创造属于我自己的东西。

1076
00:33:00.080 --> 00:33:00.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1077
00:33:00.660 --> 00:33:00.920
Yeah.
是的。

1078
00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:01.440
Right?
对吧？

1079
00:33:01.620 --> 00:33:03.140
And so you created this thing.
所以你创造了这个东西。

1080
00:33:03.200 --> 00:33:04.160
It's your own thing.
这是你自己的东西。

1081
00:33:04.380 --> 00:33:04.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1082
00:33:04.580 --> 00:33:06.420
And it's like, you're adapting.
而且就像是，你在不断适应。

1083
00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:10.320
Because it's like, I think that, obviously, it's transitioning into something else.
因为我觉得，很明显，它正在向其他方向转型。

1084
00:33:10.400 --> 00:33:13.900
We don't know really what it is with the emergence of AI and other things.
随着人工智能和其他事物的出现，我们其实并不清楚它最终会变成什么样。

1085
00:33:14.380 --> 00:33:16.940
But it's like, we're adapting to what it is.
但就像是，我们在适应眼前的现实。

1086
00:33:17.060 --> 00:33:20.420
So it's like, for you to survive this long is amazing.
所以说，你能坚持这么久真的很了不起。

1087
00:33:20.660 --> 00:33:20.960
Yeah.
是的。

1088
00:33:21.200 --> 00:33:22.500
You know, you're survivors.
你知道的，你们都是幸存者。

1089
00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:24.240
Well, thanks for saying that.
好吧，谢谢你这么说。

1090
00:33:24.740 --> 00:33:26.880
Yeah, you have to be able to adapt, right?
对，你必须具备适应能力，对吧？

1091
00:33:27.040 --> 00:33:27.280
Yeah.
是的。

1092
00:33:28.080 --> 00:33:29.860
So, what do you want to do next?
那么，你接下来想做什么？

1093
00:33:30.280 --> 00:33:32.000
I'm going to retire in three years.
我打算在三年后退休。

1094
00:33:32.460 --> 00:33:33.260
Is that true?
真的吗？

1095
00:33:33.420 --> 00:33:33.560
Yeah.
对。

1096
00:33:34.420 --> 00:33:35.260
Retire from what?
从什么行业退休？

1097
00:33:35.460 --> 00:33:35.600
Everything.
所有行业。

1098
00:33:36.120 --> 00:33:37.840
From podcasting, comedy, and acting?
从播客、喜剧到演戏？

1099
00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:38.180
Yeah, everything.
对，一切。

1100
00:33:38.380 --> 00:33:39.620
You're just going to peace out.
你只是打算拍拍屁股走人。

1101
00:33:39.680 --> 00:33:40.180
Where are you going?
你要去哪？

1102
00:33:40.920 --> 00:33:42.140
I want to go to Hawaii.
我想去夏威夷。

1103
00:33:42.480 --> 00:33:43.260
Oh, yeah.
哦，是吗。

1104
00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:45.040
And just buy a little place.
然后买个小房子。

1105
00:33:45.240 --> 00:33:45.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1106
00:33:45.620 --> 00:33:46.000
Amazing.
太棒了。

1107
00:33:46.320 --> 00:33:47.240
And just retire and farm.
然后退休去种地。

1108
00:33:47.240 --> 00:33:48.220
Yes.
对。

1109
00:33:48.540 --> 00:33:50.080
But I'm never going to do it, am I?
但我永远都不会去做，对吧？

1110
00:33:50.440 --> 00:33:51.360
Why not?
为什么不呢？

1111
00:33:51.740 --> 00:33:53.480
Because I say it, but I don't think I will.
因为我嘴上说说，但觉得不会付诸行动。

1112
00:33:53.560 --> 00:33:54.940
This is a beautiful idea.
这真是个美好的想法。

1113
00:33:55.260 --> 00:33:59.820
Don't you feel compelled to be artistic and creative, though?
不过，你难道不觉得有一种想要进行艺术创作的冲动吗？

1114
00:34:00.380 --> 00:34:04.300
Like, where will you take that energy in the Hawaii farming chapter?
比如说，你在夏威夷种地的篇章里，要把那股精力往哪放？

1115
00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:05.380
Okay, so here's what I'll do.
好吧，那我这么做。

1116
00:34:05.900 --> 00:34:07.000
This is my plan.
这是我的计划。

1117
00:34:07.320 --> 00:34:07.860
Okay?
好吗？

1118
00:34:08.160 --> 00:34:08.380
Okay.
好。

1119
00:34:08.600 --> 00:34:14.500
I'll still do my own solo podcast in Hawaii, but more ranting and raving about things.
我还是会在夏威夷做我自己的个人播客，不过会更多地对各种事情发飙和疯狂吐槽。

1120
00:34:14.780 --> 00:34:15.260
Okay.
好吧。

1121
00:34:16.080 --> 00:34:18.780
And then I'll still do local stand-up in Hawaii.
然后我依然会在夏威夷做当地的单口喜剧。

1122
00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:19.260
Okay.
行。

1123
00:34:19.600 --> 00:34:19.800
Yeah.
对。

1124
00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:22.560
And then I think that'll fill, you know, but it's like—
然后我觉得这就填补了，你知道的，但感觉——

1125
00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:23.020
It'll check your box.
这就满足了你的心愿。

1126
00:34:23.440 --> 00:34:27.920
Yeah, but I think that I've been chasing this since I was 23 years old.
对，但我觉得我从23岁开始就一直在追求这个。

1127
00:34:28.100 --> 00:34:28.480
Yeah.
对。

1128
00:34:28.480 --> 00:34:30.260
And it never seems like I made it.
而且感觉我从来没有真正成功过。

1129
00:34:30.440 --> 00:34:31.220
You made it.
你成功了。

1130
00:34:31.280 --> 00:34:32.660
I know, but it doesn't feel like it.
我知道，但感觉不像。

1131
00:34:32.940 --> 00:34:33.320
I know.
我懂。

1132
00:34:33.340 --> 00:34:34.940
Okay, I want to unpack this.
好吧，我想好好剖析一下这个。

1133
00:34:35.360 --> 00:34:38.260
What do you expect making it would feel like?
你觉得成功了应该是什么感觉？

1134
00:34:39.020 --> 00:34:39.260
What?
什么？

1135
00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:40.140
Can I be honest with you?
我能跟你说实话吗？

1136
00:34:40.220 --> 00:34:40.400
Yeah.
行。

1137
00:34:40.600 --> 00:34:40.740
Of course.
当然。

1138
00:34:40.840 --> 00:34:44.260
This is the first movie, Nimrods, where I was in the opening credits.
这是第一部电影《笨蛋》，我的名字出现在了片头字幕里。

1139
00:34:44.640 --> 00:34:44.980
Yeah.
对。

1140
00:34:45.740 --> 00:34:47.580
So thank you for that experience.
所以谢谢你让我有了这种体验。

1141
00:34:48.020 --> 00:34:48.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1142
00:34:48.220 --> 00:34:48.420
Yeah.
对。

1143
00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:51.880
I've done a lot of movies before, but I was always in the end credits.
我以前拍过很多电影，但我的名字总是在片尾字幕里。

1144
00:34:52.400 --> 00:34:54.440
And 52 names would come down.
然后有52个名字滚过。

1145
00:34:54.600 --> 00:34:57.480
And they would say, Bobby Lee, Ken Park, but, like, no one's watching.
他们会念出：鲍比·李、肯·帕克，但是，基本上没人看。

1146
00:34:57.480 --> 00:35:00.540
My point is that I've been in this business for so long.
我的意思是，我在这个行业待了这么久。

1147
00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:04.580
I've been on sitcoms and series regular, so God bless America.
我演过情景喜剧，当过剧集常规演员，所以感谢上帝保佑美国。

1148
00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:09.800
But my point is this, is that this is the first movie where I was in the opening credits.
但我的意思是，这是第一部我的名字出现在片头字幕里的电影。

1149
00:35:10.040 --> 00:35:11.340
You're on the movie poster, too.
你也在电影海报上。

1150
00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:11.680
I know.
我知道。

1151
00:35:11.740 --> 00:35:16.380
My point, though, being that I'm grateful for what I've had, but it's like this chasing thing
不过我的意思是，我很感激我曾经拥有的一切，但就像这种追逐的感觉

1152
00:35:16.380 --> 00:35:17.360
I think I'm done with.
我想我已经受够了。

1153
00:35:18.160 --> 00:35:19.860
Well, that's a real thing to listen to.
嗯，这确实是内心真实的呼唤。

1154
00:35:20.060 --> 00:35:20.800
I'm with you.
我赞同你的看法。

1155
00:35:20.920 --> 00:35:22.940
I feel tired of just—
我只是觉得厌倦了——

1156
00:35:22.940 --> 00:35:23.360
Chasing.
追逐。

1157
00:35:23.540 --> 00:35:23.860
Chasing.
追逐。

1158
00:35:23.960 --> 00:35:26.220
I don't want to be a hamster on the wheel.
我不想当转轮上的仓鼠。

1159
00:35:26.220 --> 00:35:27.560
I've been telling Jenna that.
我一直在对珍娜这么说。

1160
00:35:27.700 --> 00:35:28.560
And I'm happy.
而且我很满足。

1161
00:35:28.680 --> 00:35:31.340
And I think everything I've done is enough for me.
而且我觉得我做过的一切对我都足够了。

1162
00:35:31.800 --> 00:35:32.120
Really.
真的。

1163
00:35:33.660 --> 00:35:36.820
Happiness is a warm—yes, it is.
幸福就是温暖的——对，确实如此。

1164
00:35:37.560 --> 00:35:38.480
God—I don't know why I did this.
天哪——我不知道我为什么要这么做。

1165
00:35:38.620 --> 00:35:38.920
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1166
00:35:39.260 --> 00:35:50.180
It's more about MADtv.
这更多是关于《疯狂电视》的事。

1167
00:35:50.400 --> 00:35:51.280
What was that like?
那是怎样一种体验？

1168
00:35:52.140 --> 00:35:54.780
But you have to understand, when I was on MADtv, I'd never taken an acting class.
但你得明白，当我在《疯狂电视》的时候，我从未上过表演课。

1169
00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:55.520
I've never been on TV.
我从来没上过电视。

1170
00:35:55.640 --> 00:35:59.340
I didn't know what a jib camera was or a mark was or any of that.
我不知道什么是摇臂摄像机，什么是站位标记，什么都不知道。

1171
00:35:59.480 --> 00:35:59.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1172
00:35:59.620 --> 00:36:01.400
So you're learning how to do TV.
所以你是在边学边做电视。

1173
00:36:02.040 --> 00:36:08.120
I was an open-miker, like doing just like little rooms and like empty rooMs.
我曾经是个开放麦演员，就像在那种小场地和空荡荡的房间里表演一样。

1174
00:36:08.840 --> 00:36:10.260
No one knew who I was.
没人认识我是谁。

1175
00:36:10.820 --> 00:36:13.500
And then all of a sudden, you know, I auditioned.
然后突然之间，你知道的，我去试镜了。

1176
00:36:13.520 --> 00:36:14.920
It was a cattle call, pretty much.
那几乎是一场大规模的海选。

1177
00:36:15.040 --> 00:36:17.600
And then it came down to me and Taryn Killam.
最后在我和塔伦·基拉姆之间抉择。

1178
00:36:17.740 --> 00:36:18.360
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1179
00:36:18.500 --> 00:36:18.720
Wow.
哇。

1180
00:36:18.840 --> 00:36:20.080
And they hired both of us.
然后他们把我们两个都录用了。

1181
00:36:20.200 --> 00:36:22.020
He was on MADtv before he was on SNL.
他在加入《周六夜现场》之前就在《疯狂电视》了。

1182
00:36:22.040 --> 00:36:22.360
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1183
00:36:22.440 --> 00:36:22.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1184
00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:25.520
And then all of a sudden, I'm on a show, and I don't know how to do it.
然后突然之间，我上了一个节目，而我根本不知道该怎么演。

1185
00:36:25.700 --> 00:36:27.180
I just didn't know how to do it.
我就是不知道该怎么演。

1186
00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:28.500
How old were you?
你当时多大？

1187
00:36:29.200 --> 00:36:30.100
I was 30.
我30岁。

1188
00:36:30.460 --> 00:36:31.040
30, yeah.
30岁，对。

1189
00:36:31.740 --> 00:36:33.340
I was 30 when I booked the office.
我接下《办公室》时正好30岁。

1190
00:36:33.460 --> 00:36:33.660
Yeah.
对。

1191
00:36:33.740 --> 00:36:35.880
And I was like, how do you do this?
当时我就想，这到底该怎么演？

1192
00:36:35.980 --> 00:36:39.580
You know, I did some commercials, but it's like, those are different.
你知道的，我拍过一些广告，但那感觉不一样。

1193
00:36:39.960 --> 00:36:40.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1194
00:36:40.860 --> 00:36:44.100
Because, you know, sometimes when you're on a commercial, it's like, you'll see somebody
因为，你知道的，有时候拍广告的时候，你会看到有人

1195
00:36:44.100 --> 00:36:46.400
running by you, you just do a facial expression.
从你身边跑过，你只需做一个面部表情就行了。

1196
00:36:46.600 --> 00:36:47.220
Those I can do.
那种我还能应付。

1197
00:36:47.840 --> 00:36:48.240
Right.
没错。

1198
00:36:48.360 --> 00:36:52.600
But it's like, you know, anything with like substantial lines, you know, it would be nerve-wracking
但你知道的，任何有实质性台词的戏，对我来说

1199
00:36:52.600 --> 00:36:53.020
for me.
都会非常伤脑筋。

1200
00:36:53.640 --> 00:36:56.220
Because back then also, there was no teleprompter.
因为那个时候也没有提词器。

1201
00:36:56.580 --> 00:36:56.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1202
00:36:56.700 --> 00:37:01.860
So if I would play Connie Chung, and I had to do a monologue, it was literally learn the
所以如果我要扮演康妮·钟，还得演一段独白，那就真的是得把

1203
00:37:01.860 --> 00:37:02.340
whole thing.
整段都背下来。

1204
00:37:02.600 --> 00:37:02.920
Is that right?
是这样吗？

1205
00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:03.340
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1206
00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:04.140
Wow.
哇。

1207
00:37:04.300 --> 00:37:04.580
Wow.
哇。

1208
00:37:04.780 --> 00:37:08.300
And you're looking in the camera, and you're like, you have to memorize a page worth of
而且你得看着镜头，就好像，你得背下一整页纸的

1209
00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:09.260
things.
台词。

1210
00:37:09.260 --> 00:37:14.740
And I remember one time, one of the producers came up to me, and she held my hands, and
我记得有一次，有个制作人走到我面前，握着我的手，

1211
00:37:14.740 --> 00:37:16.400
she said, just breathe.
她说，放轻松，呼吸就行。

1212
00:37:16.680 --> 00:37:18.240
It was in front of a live audience, too.
而且那还是在现场观众面前。

1213
00:37:18.340 --> 00:37:19.140
I don't know.
我不知道。

1214
00:37:19.240 --> 00:37:19.900
I never did.
我从来没演过。

1215
00:37:20.520 --> 00:37:23.860
In high school, I maybe did some plays, but, you know, I was in The Sound of Music.
上高中时，我可能演过一些话剧，但是，你知道的，我演过《音乐之声》。

1216
00:37:24.680 --> 00:37:27.400
I played Kirk, whatever, or Kurt, whatever his name is.
我演的是柯克，随便吧，或者库尔特，管他叫什么名字呢。

1217
00:37:27.540 --> 00:37:28.800
But I played Huckleberry Finn.
但我演过哈克贝利·费恩。

1218
00:37:29.700 --> 00:37:30.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1219
00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:31.620
Why are you laughing?
你笑什么？

1220
00:37:31.780 --> 00:37:32.460
I don't know.
我不知道。

1221
00:37:33.760 --> 00:37:34.680
I juSt...
我只...

1222
00:37:34.680 --> 00:37:35.560
Can I just say something?
我能说句话吗？

1223
00:37:35.840 --> 00:37:38.000
I wish I could go back and see you in these productions.
我真希望当时能回去看你演这些作品。

1224
00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:43.640
So, when Fraulein Maria calls us for the first thing coming down the street, or I was in
所以，当玛丽亚修女叫我们做第一件事，从街上走下来的时候，或者我在

1225
00:37:43.640 --> 00:37:48.680
high school, and I was the only Korean kid in the cast, and every time the audience would
高中时，我是剧组里唯一的韩国小孩，每次观众

1226
00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:50.160
see me, the audience would laugh.
看到我，观众都会笑。

1227
00:37:50.860 --> 00:37:51.500
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1228
